Subject: [PATCH 2358/2368] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: ICP firmware
 name

The Surface Pro 11 uses the camera ICP firmware signed for it, as
shipped with its Windows camera driver.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 30d8826c967d727955f35e1a86244f46cbfb2801)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
index f6c3e3a53cf5ad62b666748eb255309fcfd09f14..7463c67ed3a02fc0fe6c7db4c4f646a521bebcbc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -1821,3 +1821,7 @@ &usb_1_ss1_dwc3_hs {
 &usb_1_ss1_qmpphy_out {
 	remote-endpoint = <&retimer_ss1_ss_in>;
 };
+
+&icp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Denali/CAMERA_ICP.mbn";
+};
